  "answer_core": "Slow the situation down, but keep a clear safety floor. Before making irreversible reporting decisions, talk with a therapist, RAINN, or legal counsel. Work with the co‑parent enough to stay aligned on safety without turning it into a blame fight, and avoid a sudden phone shutdown unless a clear tripwire fires. The tripwires are concrete: any request to meet, sexual images or talk, threats, signs the older person is also contacting other minors, a move to a hidden channel after boundaries are set, or your child saying they feel pressured or afraid. Treat a quiet or monitored phone as weak reassurance; it may only mean the contact shifted elsewhere. Within that safety frame, keep communication with your child as steady and non-punitive as possible so they will tell you when something changes.",
